{"audio": "james-04.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 126267, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1733, "text": "James, Chapter Four."}, {"start_ms": 1733, "end_ms": 4400, "text": "From whence come wars and fightings among you?"}, {"start_ms": 4400, "end_ms": 8000, "text": "come they not hence, even of your lusts that war in your members?"}, {"start_ms": 8000, "end_ms": 18533, "text": "Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye ask not."}, {"start_ms": 18533, "end_ms": 24667, "text": "Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may consume it upon your lusts."}, {"start_ms": 24667, "end_ms": 30933, "text": "Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God?"}, {"start_ms": 30933, "end_ms": 34933, "text": "whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God."}, {"start_ms": 34933, "end_ms": 40933, "text": "Do ye think that the scripture saith in vain, The spirit that dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?"}, {"start_ms": 40933, "end_ms": 42800, "text": "But he giveth more grace."}, {"start_ms": 42800, "end_ms": 48000, "text": "Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble."}, {"start_ms": 48000, "end_ms": 50667, "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God."}, {"start_ms": 50667, "end_ms": 53733, "text": "Resist the devil, and he will flee from you."}, {"start_ms": 53733, "end_ms": 56133, "text": "Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you."}, {"start_ms": 56133, "end_ms": 60000, "text": "Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded."}, {"start_ms": 60000, "end_ms": 67733, "text": "Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness."}, {"start_ms": 67733, "end_ms": 71733, "text": "Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up."}, {"start_ms": 71733, "end_ms": 74133, "text": "Speak not evil one of another, brethren."}, {"start_ms": 74133, "end_ms": 84533, "text": "He that speaketh evil of his brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge."}, {"start_ms": 84533, "end_ms": 90533, "text": "There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?"}, {"start_ms": 90533, "end_ms": 104400, "text": "Go to now, ye that say, To day or to morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy and sell, and get gain: Whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow."}, {"start_ms": 104400, "end_ms": 106267, "text": "For what is your life?"}, {"start_ms": 106267, "end_ms": 111333, "text": "It is even a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away."}, {"start_ms": 111333, "end_ms": 116667, "text": "For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that."}, {"start_ms": 116667, "end_ms": 121333, "text": "But now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil."}, {"start_ms": 121333, "end_ms": 126267, "text": "Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin."}], "words": [{"t": "James,", "s": 242, "e": 705, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 967, "e": 1270, "si": 0}, {"t": "Four.", "s": 1330, "e": 1592, "si": 0}, {"t": "From", "s": 2214, "e": 2355, "si": 1}, {"t": "whence", "s": 2395, "e": 2635, "si": 1}, {"t": "come", "s": 2675, "e": 2876, "si": 1}, {"t": "wars", "s": 2936, "e": 3257, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 3297, "e": 3397, "si": 1}, {"t": "fightings", "s": 3437, "e": 3818, "si": 1}, {"t": "among", "s": 3859, "e": 4119, "si": 1}, {"t": "you?", "s": 4159, "e": 4280, "si": 1}, {"t": "come", "s": 4621, "e": 4802, "si": 2}, {"t": "they", "s": 4802, "e": 4923, "si": 2}, {"t": "not", "s": 4963, "e": 5104, "si": 2}, {"t": "hence,", "s": 5184, "e": 5546, "si": 2}, {"t": "even", "s": 5667, "e": 5848, "si": 2}, {"t": "of", "s": 5